1
00:00:32,112 --> 00:00:33,488
Hey, you sound cheerful today.

2
00:00:37,159 --> 00:00:38,201
Are you at my place?

3
00:00:40,788 --> 00:00:42,288
I'll finish this, then I'm on my way.

4
00:01:23,914 --> 00:01:27,000
So you are not married.

5
00:01:28,252 --> 00:01:29,293
No.

6
00:01:29,294 --> 00:01:30,336
Lived together?

7
00:01:32,297 --> 00:01:35,216
No, not really.

8
00:01:36,969 --> 00:01:40,805
Never thought of marrying her
in ten years?

9
00:01:42,850 --> 00:01:43,850
Well...

10
00:01:45,644 --> 00:01:47,145
She wanted to pursue her career.

11
00:01:49,273 --> 00:01:50,273
She what?

12
00:01:51,900 --> 00:01:52,900
Are you sure?

13
00:01:56,196 --> 00:01:57,822
But how did she get it?

14
00:02:01,702 --> 00:02:05,121
That's her friend.
I know him.

15
00:02:06,999 --> 00:02:09,500
I didn't know he was associated
with gangsters.

16
00:02:11,712 --> 00:02:13,254
I don't think she knew it.

17
00:02:14,631 --> 00:02:16,340
He may've been in trouble...

18
00:02:17,134 --> 00:02:19,719
...so left it in her care
without telling her what it was.

19
00:02:21,472 --> 00:02:24,891
Drugs?
You mean like cocaine?

20
00:02:25,726 --> 00:02:26,726
Did you find any?

21
00:02:27,227 --> 00:02:29,604
Not really.

22
00:02:31,648 --> 00:02:32,648
I don't know.

23
00:02:34,693 --> 00:02:35,693
No, I don't.

24
00:02:37,321 --> 00:02:38,738
I really don't know.

25
00:02:43,952 --> 00:02:51,952
Why?...

26
00:02:58,092 --> 00:02:59,092
Why commit suicide?

27
00:04:11,874 --> 00:04:15,042
Hello...
Where have you been?

28
00:04:15,878 --> 00:04:18,379
Stop turning off your mobile when you drink

29
00:04:19,173 --> 00:04:21,465
Need to talk about clients
screening tomorrow.

30
00:04:50,037 --> 00:04:51,037
What?

31
00:04:52,164 --> 00:04:53,414
Don't you remember me?

32
00:04:54,708 --> 00:04:58,294
You bit my hand
and left this scar.

33
00:05:01,632 --> 00:05:03,132
You staggered at the platform...

34
00:05:03,967 --> 00:05:08,054
and were almost hit by a train.
So I grabbed you, remember?

35
00:05:23,820 --> 00:05:24,820
Hey.

36
00:05:25,739 --> 00:05:27,114
What was going on then?

37
00:05:30,702 --> 00:05:31,953
What do you want?

38
00:05:33,622 --> 00:05:34,664
Wanna do 'it', or what?

39
00:05:36,291 --> 00:05:38,251
Sex. Don't you know?

40
00:05:49,638 --> 00:05:51,722
Guys, someone wants to have sex with me.

41
00:06:04,069 --> 00:06:05,069
Hi.

42
00:06:06,446 --> 00:06:07,446
Nice to see ya.

43
00:06:09,658 --> 00:06:14,287
Listen up...
I've got an early day tomorrow,

44
00:06:15,580 --> 00:06:18,207
but I've got no time to play
with kids like you.

45
00:06:19,084 --> 00:06:21,919
On top of that, I've got no money, Sonny.

46
00:06:36,560 --> 00:06:37,727
I paid you back.

47
00:06:38,562 --> 00:06:39,562
Paid back.

48
00:06:46,069 --> 00:06:48,154
I think we robbed this guy before.

49
00:06:48,655 --> 00:06:51,282
- Yeah, we sure did.
- We were playing the 'subway game'.

50
00:06:52,617 --> 00:06:53,617
It was Chisato's turn.

51
00:06:54,286 --> 00:06:56,704
He threw us his wallet
and ran away like a dog.

52
00:06:57,164 --> 00:06:58,789
What's it with you today, pop?

53
00:07:01,293 --> 00:07:02,543
Stand up.

54
00:07:04,713 --> 00:07:08,924
Bring your money to our club.

55
00:07:09,801 --> 00:07:12,553
You shouldn't tell him where.

56
00:07:13,096 --> 00:07:15,723
Oh, he means no harm to us.

57
00:07:16,767 --> 00:07:17,933
'Cause he's a chicken shit.

58
00:07:22,773 --> 00:07:27,193
Don't do anything funny,
or you'll be in trouble.

59
00:07:28,862 --> 00:07:30,363
I'm already in deep shit.

60
00:07:31,823 --> 00:07:33,282
Even a worm turns, so to speak

61
00:07:34,618 --> 00:07:36,702
Ain't that right, Chisato?

62
00:07:48,215 --> 00:07:49,215
Kiriko...

63
00:07:57,140 --> 00:07:59,100
how did you get the gun?

64
00:08:02,104 --> 00:08:04,188
How the hell did you get it?

65
00:08:17,786 --> 00:08:18,786
What's so funny?

66
00:08:19,121 --> 00:08:20,830
Our clients looked very satisfied.

67
00:08:21,164 --> 00:08:24,708
My grand daughter's eyes are glued
to the TV whenever...

68
00:08:24,709 --> 00:08:25,918
your commercials are on.

69
00:08:26,336 --> 00:08:29,338
Goda, make yourself available
for next one, will you?

70
00:08:29,631 --> 00:08:30,631
Sure.

71
00:08:30,882 --> 00:08:32,925
- Well, then...
- See you.

72
00:08:41,059 --> 00:08:42,476
He looks better.

73
00:08:43,353 --> 00:08:47,189
Even at the loss of his girlfriend,
he doesn't take even a day off.

74
00:08:52,362 --> 00:08:53,737
- You know...
- Yes?

75
00:08:55,699 --> 00:08:58,367
How does one get a gun here?

76
00:08:59,494 --> 00:09:00,494
What?

77
00:09:02,622 --> 00:09:03,622
Oh that...

78
00:09:08,795 --> 00:09:10,296
"Toy Gun Shop"

79
00:09:27,355 --> 00:09:30,774
Shut your goddamn mouth up.

80
00:09:34,988 --> 00:09:35,988
Sorry!

81
00:09:36,656 --> 00:09:39,074
- Hold it right there.
- Ok.

82
00:09:45,207 --> 00:09:47,791
You got any idea how much a gun costs?

83
00:09:48,460 --> 00:09:49,460
How much?

84
00:09:51,546 --> 00:09:56,884
2 million for a gun and
500,000 yen for 5 bullets.

85
00:09:59,137 --> 00:10:00,846
How much is it all together?

86
00:10:01,848 --> 00:10:02,932
2.5 million yen.

87
00:10:04,184 --> 00:10:05,351
You got that right.

88
00:10:07,187 --> 00:10:09,063
I'll get you the money tomorrow morning.

89
00:10:09,648 --> 00:10:13,275
This is a deposit.

90
00:10:15,904 --> 00:10:16,904
Umm...

91
00:10:18,740 --> 00:10:20,658
You got a 'chief special'?

92
00:10:26,248 --> 00:10:29,083
This is strictly between us.

93
00:10:29,918 --> 00:10:32,545
If you got any problem,
come to me first.

94
00:10:32,963 --> 00:10:35,798
Don't talk with anyone in the syndicate.

95
00:11:34,149 --> 00:11:36,525
How has your son worked out so far?

96
00:11:37,110 --> 00:11:38,152
He's just fine.

97
00:11:40,071 --> 00:11:44,533
He used to be wild and got into fights...

98
00:11:45,076 --> 00:11:46,702
when he was your son's age.

99
00:11:47,162 --> 00:11:50,664
Me?
I don't remember.

100
00:11:51,207 --> 00:11:53,042
You don't say.

101
00:11:55,837 --> 00:11:59,840
But I think no one could've kicked
your ass when you were that age.

102
00:12:01,176 --> 00:12:03,010
I was much younger.

103
00:12:05,096 --> 00:12:06,889
The time was right after World War II.

104
00:12:07,265 --> 00:12:09,850
No training needed then,
it was the way of life.

105
00:12:10,560 --> 00:12:12,061
So much for my past.

106
00:12:15,607 --> 00:12:17,358
You came to see my son?

107
00:12:20,278 --> 00:12:22,863
Come on in.
Shigeo, your friends are here.

108
00:12:28,703 --> 00:12:31,080
Hi. Please take this.

109
00:12:32,207 --> 00:12:34,708
When you gonna rob somebody,
make sure he's weaker.

110
00:12:37,003 --> 00:12:39,046
Thanks for your help then.

111
00:12:55,438 --> 00:12:57,022
'Chief Special'

112
00:13:17,085 --> 00:13:21,171
No, no. I don't have it,
but I've got 'speed' and 'weed'

113
00:13:22,132 --> 00:13:23,173
What's 'speed'?

114
00:13:23,174 --> 00:13:24,174
It's 'shabu'.

115
00:13:25,009 --> 00:13:26,677
You mean methedrine?

116
00:13:33,184 --> 00:13:34,184
Good evening.

117
00:14:01,045 --> 00:14:06,550
Thought you were at work. What's this?

118
00:14:25,737 --> 00:14:29,865
Ringo Kid: Dismantle a gun.
Use tin foil to pass the custom check.

119
00:14:30,200 --> 00:14:34,453
Jun Wayne: Import some parts,
then you can reassemble a gun.

120
00:14:34,704 --> 00:14:40,292
Better Tomorrow: Someone made
a real gun out of an old toy.

121
00:14:44,088 --> 00:14:45,756
You mean illegally made?

122
00:15:02,106 --> 00:15:03,440
Can't give you a receipt.

123
00:15:04,234 --> 00:15:06,902
It's a toy gun, right?
Don't make any trouble for me.

124
00:15:09,781 --> 00:15:11,990
The same size as this?

125
00:15:12,367 --> 00:15:14,993
Yes, the size of a pencil holder.

126
00:15:15,286 --> 00:15:19,748
This, too, the same size,
using this material...

127
00:15:19,999 --> 00:15:20,999
I see.

128
00:15:22,085 --> 00:15:24,711
I want to use it for a long time.
So please make it strong.

129
00:18:21,472 --> 00:18:24,266
Wow, Idei gave us a lot.

130
00:18:25,101 --> 00:18:27,269
Don't be an 'amateur'.

131
00:18:27,854 --> 00:18:30,188
Here is your ticket to heaven.

132
00:18:31,024 --> 00:18:33,859
You should try this, Goto.

133
00:19:18,654 --> 00:19:19,988
I got it, Sugar.

134
00:19:20,907 --> 00:19:22,824
You're stuck with real hard job, Honey.

135
00:19:24,243 --> 00:19:27,454
It ain't a Utopia here.

136
00:19:29,248 --> 00:19:32,834
Forget about ideal.
Then you start to feel better.

137
00:20:08,246 --> 00:20:10,831
You got the money, pop. Good!

138
00:20:11,666 --> 00:20:14,000
Where the hell are they?
Tell me!

139
00:20:17,839 --> 00:20:19,798
I'll break their necks!

140
00:21:16,063 --> 00:21:17,564
What's going on there?

141
00:21:35,541 --> 00:21:36,708
That hurts, man!

142
00:22:35,685 --> 00:22:37,811
Don't make the scene at my club.

143
00:22:40,815 --> 00:22:42,983
Who's this guy?

144
00:22:44,318 --> 00:22:45,443
He's nobody.

145
00:22:47,780 --> 00:22:49,447
Get outta here, jerk!

146
00:23:26,110 --> 00:23:28,111
- Did that jerk scare you?
- Not a chance.

147
00:23:29,447 --> 00:23:30,780
Good girl, good.

148
00:23:32,825 --> 00:23:34,743
How did you get this scar?

149
00:23:35,036 --> 00:23:36,202
I got it recently.

150
00:23:36,954 --> 00:23:38,997
The best I've ever felt.

151
00:23:39,457 --> 00:23:40,582
I threw myself...

152
00:23:42,418 --> 00:23:43,418
into a moving car.

153
00:23:46,297 --> 00:23:47,422
What about this?

154
00:23:47,715 --> 00:23:50,967
That's nothing.
A punk stabbed me with a knife.

155
00:23:53,054 --> 00:23:55,889
Why do you take speed alone?

156
00:24:01,228 --> 00:24:03,313
I don't want anyone to see me...

157
00:24:03,689 --> 00:24:06,066
just like I'm eating or having sex.

158
00:24:30,257 --> 00:24:31,257
You'll die...

159
00:25:12,508 --> 00:25:18,221
'Chisato Will Die at Midnight Tomorrow'

160
00:25:26,313 --> 00:25:28,398
Who the hell cares!

161
00:25:40,953 --> 00:25:43,621
What do you want from me?

162
00:25:46,625 --> 00:25:48,293
What's it about tomorrow?

163
00:25:50,796 --> 00:25:52,714
None of your business.

164
00:25:56,135 --> 00:25:57,677
Tell me what'll happen?

165
00:26:07,855 --> 00:26:11,316
It's a group of punks.
They're pushing us around...

166
00:26:14,820 --> 00:26:16,988
so we'll whack 'em.

167
00:26:19,033 --> 00:26:20,033
Where is it?

168
00:26:21,160 --> 00:26:23,703
You want a day off?

169
00:26:25,748 --> 00:26:27,916
You want me to tell it to our boss?

170
00:26:29,335 --> 00:26:31,711
Are you out of your mind?
Goda... hello...

171
00:27:47,079 --> 00:27:48,079
Hey!

172
00:27:49,957 --> 00:27:50,957
You!

173
00:27:53,168 --> 00:27:54,669
What's going on there?

174
00:27:59,550 --> 00:28:01,467
What's that shitty face for?

175
00:28:01,844 --> 00:28:04,387
Who the hell you think that car belongs to?

176
00:28:33,584 --> 00:28:37,462
Get rid of him fast.
Shit! He's fucking heavy.

177
00:28:59,443 --> 00:29:00,443
Me?

178
00:29:01,403 --> 00:29:02,945
I'll find work like anybody else.

179
00:29:03,906 --> 00:29:05,657
Can't go on like this forever.

180
00:29:07,451 --> 00:29:09,911
I'll go to college
to study science and engineering.

181
00:29:13,916 --> 00:29:15,124
- You know what?
- What?

182
00:29:16,418 --> 00:29:20,963
I'll bring a bat with lots of
nails stuck in as a weapon.

183
00:29:22,549 --> 00:29:23,675
How about yours?

184
00:29:24,677 --> 00:29:25,677
Mine?

185
00:29:26,387 --> 00:29:29,722
My fists will do.
I'll blow 'em away with my punches.

186
00:29:38,857 --> 00:29:41,275
- Hope we can work together.
- I do, too.

187
00:29:41,777 --> 00:29:44,487
I am off this way.
See you.

188
00:30:21,608 --> 00:30:22,608
Listen, Goto.

189
00:30:23,444 --> 00:30:26,863
Teach those punks a real lesson tonight.

190
00:30:28,157 --> 00:30:30,199
Show 'em how serious we are.

191
00:30:33,370 --> 00:30:35,538
You ain't scared, are you?!

192
00:30:37,541 --> 00:30:38,541
Idei...

193
00:30:40,544 --> 00:30:41,836
...I'll kill 'em for sure.

194
00:30:45,424 --> 00:30:47,216
I was told you've got guns!

195
00:30:47,217 --> 00:30:49,260
Give me a break!
No guns here.

196
00:30:49,636 --> 00:30:51,012
Please! Sell one to me!

197
00:30:51,430 --> 00:30:54,724
I want a 'Chief Special'.
I need it!

198
00:31:22,544 --> 00:31:25,797
I've been watching you.

199
00:31:28,091 --> 00:31:31,093
You'll get this if you do me a favour.

200
00:31:34,640 --> 00:31:35,640
Marry me.

201
00:31:39,520 --> 00:31:41,646
I can't go back to my country now.

202
00:31:42,064 --> 00:31:46,567
I need more money to live here.

203
00:31:47,945 --> 00:31:48,945
More and more.

204
00:31:49,530 --> 00:31:54,992
I need a visa to stay here,
so getting married is the answer.

205
00:31:56,161 --> 00:31:57,745
Let me ask you a question.

206
00:32:00,791 --> 00:32:03,000
Was it his gun,
the guy who was killed?

207
00:32:05,379 --> 00:32:07,672
He said to forget him if he died.

208
00:32:08,632 --> 00:32:12,301
That's what I am doing now.

209
00:32:16,682 --> 00:32:19,600
Do I sign and put my stamp here

210
00:32:24,773 --> 00:32:28,150
I can be your 'wife' sometimes.

211
00:32:40,247 --> 00:32:42,290
This is our wedding ceremony.

212
00:33:29,588 --> 00:33:30,588
Kiriko...

213
00:35:43,430 --> 00:35:45,264
There're a lot more punks than us.

214
00:35:46,308 --> 00:35:48,768
We'll manage.
It's a matter of when we hit 'em.

215
00:35:49,561 --> 00:35:53,856
Listen, Goda. You take care of that
tough lookin' guy.

216
00:35:54,191 --> 00:35:55,733
Forget about the rest.

217
00:35:56,860 --> 00:36:00,821
Well, let's see... you and you...

218
00:36:45,617 --> 00:36:50,538
Move your asses now.
You get back in the car.

219
00:36:51,206 --> 00:36:53,791
Hey, get back and stay there.

220
00:37:37,586 --> 00:37:39,587
Meet me at our base!

221
00:37:42,507 --> 00:37:43,883
Meet me there, guys!

222
00:37:57,772 --> 00:38:01,734
I'm coming you, Sucker!
Get ready for my fists.

223
00:38:18,752 --> 00:38:19,960
Here they come!

224
00:39:09,010 --> 00:39:10,344
Take that shortcut!

225
00:40:18,621 --> 00:40:20,289
These guys got no guts.

226
00:41:46,751 --> 00:41:48,085
'CHISATO WILL DIE'

227
00:41:49,045 --> 00:41:50,295
Hold it right there!

228
00:42:30,420 --> 00:42:31,545
Let's see...

229
00:42:32,589 --> 00:42:35,716
So it looks like we got into a gun fight.

230
00:42:36,968 --> 00:42:37,968
In that case...

231
00:42:39,012 --> 00:42:41,722
Carry this guy to my club.

232
00:42:44,350 --> 00:42:47,186
Take this one back to his place.

233
00:42:48,188 --> 00:42:50,814
Chisato and Goto, you do that.

234
00:42:56,196 --> 00:42:58,155
Don't take him to hospital.

235
00:43:04,287 --> 00:43:06,121
Make sure you grab that thing...

236
00:43:08,625 --> 00:43:09,750
on your way out.

237
00:43:28,853 --> 00:43:29,853
Hey...

238
00:43:33,107 --> 00:43:34,608
You wanna die?

239
00:43:42,158 --> 00:43:43,909
Did you send this to Goto?

240
00:43:45,119 --> 00:43:49,122
I've been watching you.
Who did you send it to?

241
00:43:57,298 --> 00:43:59,508
Take it easy on that speed, will you?

242
00:44:01,844 --> 00:44:02,844
I never touch.

243
00:44:03,721 --> 00:44:04,721
What?

244
00:44:05,431 --> 00:44:10,811
That shit.
I've never done it.

245
00:44:14,107 --> 00:44:15,399
What's on your mind?

246
00:44:19,404 --> 00:44:20,988
Don't go too far.

247
00:44:23,533 --> 00:44:24,908
What do you care?

248
00:44:47,348 --> 00:44:51,059
Why are you...
always in the fast lane?

249
00:44:52,228 --> 00:44:53,520
Mind your own business.

250
00:44:57,066 --> 00:45:01,778
My girlfriend...
died here.

251
00:45:03,948 --> 00:45:07,492
Why did she...

252
00:45:10,705 --> 00:45:11,913
kill herself?

253
00:45:26,012 --> 00:45:28,847
All right, sucker! I tell you why.

254
00:45:29,849 --> 00:45:31,767
It was you who killed her.

255
00:45:32,810 --> 00:45:33,894
It's your fault.

256
00:45:35,480 --> 00:45:38,523
You don't know you're such
a selfish bastard!

257
00:45:38,941 --> 00:45:41,485
You care only about yourself and...

258
00:45:41,486 --> 00:45:43,945
will never understand her feelings.

259
00:45:44,781 --> 00:45:46,573
But then again, it's not only you.

260
00:45:47,158 --> 00:45:52,412
I know there're many people
like you in this world.

261
00:45:53,039 --> 00:45:54,748
They all killed her.

262
00:46:00,922 --> 00:46:01,922
Go ahead.

263
00:46:07,762 --> 00:46:08,970
Pull the trigger!

264
00:46:25,905 --> 00:46:26,988
Do it yourself.

265
00:47:16,497 --> 00:47:18,749
No, I didn't mean it.

266
00:47:19,709 --> 00:47:20,792
Like you said...

267
00:47:21,878 --> 00:47:25,130
I am the one who
didn't want to get married

268
00:47:25,465 --> 00:47:28,550
Never mind. It's not your fault.

269
00:47:34,515 --> 00:47:38,351
I've never taken marriage seriously.

270
00:47:40,313 --> 00:47:45,525
I think I've been trying not
to see things that are important to me.

271
00:47:47,487 --> 00:47:52,115
People have kids because they need
a reason to keep living.

272
00:47:55,453 --> 00:47:59,956
Or else I'll get lost just like a kite
in the wind without a string.

273
00:48:21,938 --> 00:48:24,231
This is an answering machine...

274
00:48:25,566 --> 00:48:30,070
...so please leave your
message after the tone.

275
00:48:32,031 --> 00:48:34,199
Goda, it's about the assignments.

276
00:48:34,408 --> 00:48:36,368
I found a director to do the commercials.

277
00:49:00,309 --> 00:49:01,309
Kiriko...

278
00:49:03,813 --> 00:49:06,481
my string...
will break soon.

279
00:49:08,609 --> 00:49:09,609
Let's have...

280
00:49:12,113 --> 00:49:13,113
our own kid.

281
00:50:34,987 --> 00:50:36,655
Give us your money now!

282
00:50:37,990 --> 00:50:39,741
Who do you think you are?

283
00:50:41,452 --> 00:50:42,452
Grab it.

284
00:51:08,771 --> 00:51:11,231
Hey, the whole town knows
what you're doing.

285
00:51:13,651 --> 00:51:14,651
Keep it down...

286
00:51:15,277 --> 00:51:16,277
...will you?

287
00:51:16,946 --> 00:51:23,743
Go out and shoot the bum
under the highway.

288
00:51:23,995 --> 00:51:26,037
That bum stinks.

289
00:51:28,457 --> 00:51:29,457
Do it quietly.

290
00:51:36,257 --> 00:51:40,176
Goto, you go.
Congratulations on your job.

291
00:51:43,681 --> 00:51:46,016
Who you're staring at?
We all know about it.

292
00:51:47,059 --> 00:51:49,310
A business suit will look good on you.

293
00:51:50,730 --> 00:51:53,648
Never mind the bum.
Kill anyone who disgusts you...

294
00:51:55,568 --> 00:51:57,527
and then you can redeem
your honour.

295
00:52:01,615 --> 00:52:04,159
In your dreams,
you kill people but don't get caught.

296
00:52:06,162 --> 00:52:08,246
The whole thing about Tokyo is a dream.

297
00:52:09,331 --> 00:52:10,790
We are all in the fucking dream.

298
00:52:21,761 --> 00:52:25,430
...please leave your
message after the tone.

299
00:52:26,515 --> 00:52:27,515
Hello...

300
00:53:05,137 --> 00:53:06,387
Goto has been standing...

301
00:53:08,182 --> 00:53:12,477
at a place with a gun in his hand
for an hour.

302
00:53:15,397 --> 00:53:19,734
If he gets caught with the gun...

303
00:53:21,195 --> 00:53:22,904
you will never get it again.

304
00:53:25,366 --> 00:53:26,699
You care less now?

305
00:53:33,833 --> 00:53:34,833
No...

306
00:53:37,044 --> 00:53:38,044
...I do care.

307
00:53:40,089 --> 00:53:41,089
I need it for once.

308
00:53:58,774 --> 00:53:59,858
Where is he now?

309
00:53:59,859 --> 00:54:00,817
In front of a police station.

310
00:54:00,985 --> 00:54:02,235
Are you sure about that?

311
00:54:03,070 --> 00:54:04,320
Of course I am.

312
00:54:27,845 --> 00:54:28,845
I'm here now.

313
00:54:30,139 --> 00:54:31,264
He's right there.

314
00:54:32,308 --> 00:54:34,267
Goto was riding his bicycle...

315
00:54:34,268 --> 00:54:35,685
...but that cop thought he stole it

316
00:54:36,478 --> 00:54:38,188
and treated him like a criminal.

317
00:54:40,191 --> 00:54:42,400
The cop is just a dirty-mind
in a uniform.

318
00:54:43,152 --> 00:54:46,613
Goto hates a man in uniform
who looks down on others.

319
00:55:22,024 --> 00:55:23,024
Hey, you!

320
00:55:23,651 --> 00:55:24,651
Hold it right there.

321
00:55:26,987 --> 00:55:27,987
Yes?

322
00:55:29,740 --> 00:55:32,033
There you are again.

323
00:55:36,747 --> 00:55:39,374
That bicycle looks different
to the one you had before.

324
00:55:40,251 --> 00:55:41,501
Where to?

325
00:55:46,048 --> 00:55:47,048
Come over here.

326
00:55:48,842 --> 00:55:50,176
Come here, I said.

327
00:55:52,263 --> 00:55:53,554
You come here.

328
00:55:57,059 --> 00:55:58,434
You say what?

329
00:56:09,363 --> 00:56:10,530
Let see...

330
00:56:12,324 --> 00:56:14,951
You covered the registration number
with paint here.

331
00:56:16,328 --> 00:56:18,204
See? I can't let you go free.

332
00:56:20,916 --> 00:56:22,333
You'd better come with me.

333
00:56:23,836 --> 00:56:26,504
Let's talk somewhere else.

334
00:56:29,049 --> 00:56:34,178
Shut the fuck up. My time is too
precious for a punk like you.

335
00:56:35,681 --> 00:56:36,681
Excuse me...

336
00:56:40,519 --> 00:56:41,519
That punk!

337
00:57:53,300 --> 00:57:54,300
Hello.

338
00:59:15,299 --> 00:59:16,382
Stop this shit.

339
00:59:20,053 --> 00:59:22,180
Give it to me.
That's mine.

340
00:59:24,016 --> 00:59:25,016
No way.

341
00:59:30,647 --> 00:59:31,731
Maybe you'll do.

342
01:00:07,476 --> 01:00:08,476
Shit!

343
01:00:15,275 --> 01:00:19,737
I'm in chaos.
It would be easier to give the gun back.

344
01:00:39,132 --> 01:00:42,677
It takes years of training to turn
one's body into iron like yours.

345
01:01:04,116 --> 01:01:05,283
Where the hell are you?

346
01:01:07,953 --> 01:01:09,912
Hey, tell me!

347
01:01:10,914 --> 01:01:11,914
Hey!

348
01:02:18,023 --> 01:02:19,065
Gang's fight?

349
01:02:19,775 --> 01:02:21,359
A boxer was shot to death.

350
01:02:23,111 --> 01:02:24,111
A boxer!

351
01:05:52,737 --> 01:05:57,491
Our business has made us a lot of enemies.

352
01:06:00,078 --> 01:06:01,412
But in this case...

353
01:06:03,748 --> 01:06:07,209
shooting the boxer
just might be the end of all of us.

354
01:06:08,628 --> 01:06:14,008
Radar captures our movements
by 0. I seconds and...

355
01:06:14,593 --> 01:06:18,721
calculates the subsequent moves
up to two years in a row.

356
01:06:19,848 --> 01:06:22,349
That means we can't fight our destiny.

357
01:06:48,209 --> 01:06:49,209
The door...

358
01:06:50,462 --> 01:06:51,587
was open.

359
01:06:57,552 --> 01:06:58,552
I want to...

360
01:06:59,554 --> 01:07:00,638
ask you a favour.

361
01:07:15,612 --> 01:07:17,071
Two of our guys were killed.

362
01:07:17,489 --> 01:07:19,823
The rest can't step out of the club.

363
01:07:20,283 --> 01:07:23,494
It's only a matter of time
'till the shooter finds us.

364
01:07:23,787 --> 01:07:27,331
- Is it too much to ask of you to join
me against the shooter? - I'll do it.

365
01:08:38,319 --> 01:08:39,319
I'm scared.

366
01:08:41,531 --> 01:08:43,115
We won't do it then.

367
01:08:44,200 --> 01:08:45,200
It's not that.

368
01:08:45,785 --> 01:08:48,912
I am scared 'cause what if I make it?
What's next?

369
01:11:35,663 --> 01:11:39,082
You don't know what you're doing!

370
01:11:40,293 --> 01:11:41,418
Why him?!

371
01:11:41,794 --> 01:11:44,421
Do you really think he'd be any help?

372
01:11:45,465 --> 01:11:47,883
You gave him the gun!

373
01:11:49,052 --> 01:11:51,386
He may be the one who killed our friends!

374
01:11:52,222 --> 01:11:53,722
Do you hear me?!

375
01:11:53,932 --> 01:11:56,308
Don't worry,
I won't use it on you.

376
01:12:00,021 --> 01:12:01,396
Let him help us.

377
01:12:02,690 --> 01:12:04,441
If that's what he wants to do.

378
01:12:06,986 --> 01:12:08,445
You'd better do what you like.

379
01:12:09,572 --> 01:12:16,495
We're stuck in an endless game.

380
01:13:20,310 --> 01:13:21,810
What's wrong with you?!

381
01:13:57,638 --> 01:14:00,015
Hey, Chisato.

382
01:14:02,477 --> 01:14:03,602
You'd better take a rest.

383
01:15:35,653 --> 01:15:36,653
Hey.

384
01:16:43,721 --> 01:16:46,473
No, mum!
I won't be home for dinner.

385
01:17:12,583 --> 01:17:13,583
Kids...

386
01:17:14,794 --> 01:17:16,711
don't play bad games.

387
01:21:16,160 --> 01:21:17,160
Well...

388
01:21:23,042 --> 01:21:24,459
let's get outta here.

389
01:21:51,570 --> 01:21:56,741
So long.

